#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068559 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068705 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b04beff-987b-504f-9783-4465474e01ab" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "d659780a-f726-5827-a13a-a64b21a0cf41" :question/math-academy-id "e-4027" :question/problem "What are the solutions to $x^2 + 16 = 0$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} x^2 + 16 &= 0 \\\\[3pt] x^2 &= -16 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = \\pm \\sqrt{-16}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit\n\n$$\n\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= ± \\sqrt{-16} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{16 \\cdot (-1)} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{16} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± 4\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx = \\pm 4 \\textrm{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "386bce9a-0c89-545c-b9ed-b9f67fb836b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions With Simplification"}] :question/id #uuid "8082e3bd-04dc-5598-93c5-dbc423cdba97" :question/math-academy-id "e-4028" :question/problem "If $p^2 + 27 = 0$, then $p =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} p^2 + 27 & = 0 \\\\[3pt] p^2 & = -27 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\np = \\pm \\sqrt{-27}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit\n\n$$\n\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np &= ± \\sqrt{-27} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{27 \\cdot (-1)} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{27} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{3^{2} \\cdot 3} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± 3\\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± 3\\sqrt{3}\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\np = \\pm 3\\sqrt{3} \\, \\textrm{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "701015d7-cc6a-52ff-b40d-627a640cd0fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "99f522f8-39ff-5612-86d1-84e703bde35f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4029" :question/problem "If $16z^2 + 49 = 0$, then $z =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 16z^2 + 49 & = 0 \\\\[5pt] 16z^2 & = -49 \\\\[5pt] z^2 & = -\\dfrac{49}{16} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nz = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{49}{16}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit\n\n$$\n\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= ± \\sqrt{-\\frac{49}{16}} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16} \\cdot (-1)} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{16}} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{7}{4}\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\nz=\\pm \\dfrac{7}{4} \\textrm{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc45bf8f-2f0f-5ab9-b7d4-e9a3300b52a6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Roots With Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "93aec687-49af-55ea-9212-b33dd29f4ce7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4030" :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $2y^2 + 9 = 0$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2y^2 + 9 &= 0 \\\\[5pt] 2y^2 &= -9 \\\\[5pt] y^2 & = -\\dfrac{9}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain\n\n$$\ny = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{9}{2}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit\n\n$$\n\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= ± \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2} \\cdot (-1)} \\\\\n&= ± \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= ± \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\textrm{i} \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\textrm{i}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc45bf8f-2f0f-5ab9-b7d4-e9a3300b52a6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Roots With Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0931ae2-58cb-5f0a-afcb-1cce3c5c5a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067793} {:answer/id #uuid "e897336a-98c4-5bd2-8c93-9f6e1390a967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\sqrt{3}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067794} {:answer/id #uuid "237397e0-fec2-5b57-88a8-fcf7e9551eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067795} {:answer/id #uuid "27fa1851-746e-53dd-aa13-e0d902f7cbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067796} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2d87c6-2f40-5d02-b742-c4cd5f1bc4ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067797}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ab495d5c-1e27-5baa-8e34-728ab73fbe3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067792}] :question/id #uuid "47b94063-7f34-5826-9273-858fa9727be7" :question/math-academy-id "q-54630" :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $8y^{2} + 12 = 0$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "701015d7-cc6a-52ff-b40d-627a640cd0fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f936da9-a646-572f-9d19-599517423146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{5}{6}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068027} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc8d08b-826c-5bde-a69a-12c79e397cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068028} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee20fd1-455d-5f0e-b6e1-e8bd5123b8db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068029} {:answer/id #uuid "13f74ec9-b3e2-592c-9d7d-428e27523b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068030} {:answer/id #uuid "1718ea13-1349-57ff-8005-5862e053d80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "± \\frac{6}{5}\\textrm{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068031}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fb97819c-0e4a-5ac6-a889-9c7ec737b994" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068026}] :question/id #uuid "0e3bf3f1-d937-55da-b28c-d65551dd4623" :question/math-academy-id "q-66254" :question/problem "Find the solutions of the equation $25z^{2} + 36 = 0$."}]}
